===== final-1.txt
**Status: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS.** The three spec scenarios pass, but beta's unit suite fails on this node's default `python3` (3.6.8).

The run used commit set space 5d5d5d5, alpha d4d4d4d, beta e5e5e5e and gamma c3c3c3c (gamma at its pin), in env class `any`. Total wall time was about 1 s.

| Check | Result | What I saw |
|---|---|---|
| R1.S1 default greeting | pass | It returned `'hello, demo'` and exited 0 |
| R1.S2 name too long | pass | It exited 1 with nothing on standard output; the error names the 64-character limit |
| R2.S1 start-up line | pass | First line was `hello, demo`, in 0.04 s (limit: under 1 s) |
| alpha unit suite | pass | 3 tests |
| beta unit suite | **fail** | 2 errors |
| Regression suite `tests/` | no results | It holds only `.gitkeep` |
| Quality checks | none run | The spec has no Quality section (`quality: none-declared`) |

**The beta failure:** both tests call `subprocess.run(capture_output=...)`. Python 3.6 doesn't accept that keyword (it needs 3.7 or later), so both raise `TypeError` before checking anything. I re-ran the suite under `python3.12` on the same node to diagnose it, and it passed. The test is fragile, but the behavior is fine: R2.S1 passes even on 3.6.8. The fix is either to require Python 3.7+ for env class `any`, or to drop that keyword from the suite. I edited neither the test nor the code.

**Other concerns:**
- The brief puts the report at `tasks/T7-report.md`, but my role says a test task's report goes under `evidence/` and never under `tasks/`. I followed the role.
- No actor handle was given, so I used `demo/test` (the project name). Correct it if the pod uses another handle.

